{"kind":"request","text":"Make addressed ephemeral conversation a first-class, recipient-aware live signal instead of an opaque frame change that readers must rediscover by polling every conversation. Today `say` signs only `{about,text,re?}`; nexus change history reports only conversation and sequence; MCP `status` omits current addressed chat; MCP `wait` returns raw live change handles without the message or recipient semantics; and only publishing sessions are retained as conversation participants. Consequently a present `@planner` recipient can miss the message until an arbitrary later poll, can lose it when the sender leaves, and receives no trustworthy indication that the chat is theirs.\n\nResolve mentions against the effective roster at publication time and record the resolved fingerprints in the signed frame payload while retaining the authored text. A reply must also address the author of the exact parent frame, without requiring a repeated textual mention. Unknown or ambiguous mention tokens remain ordinary text and must not create false recipients. The nexus must enroll live sessions of resolved recipients as conversation participants so an addressed conversation remains available while either its sender or an addressed live recipient remains leased; do not enroll the whole room or turn ephemeral speech durable.\n\nExpose a bounded, actor-oriented ephemeral inbox through the service and MCP adapter. `wait` must return newly addressed frames inline with actor, text, about anchor, conversation, sequence, reply target, resolved recipients, and an exact thread handle; an agent must not need an unexposed frames endpoint or an N-conversation scan to learn what was said. `status` must include the bounded current addressed inbox for this adapter session, so taking a fresh orientation after a message was published does not silently advance past it. Delivery/acknowledgement state is leased and ephemeral, scoped to the exact actor session, and repeated until explicitly acknowledged or the conversation expires; it is not a durable request, promise, read receipt, or authority signal. Define reset, expiry, cap, skipped-count, replay, duplicate, self-message, multi-session, identity-switch, reply, and malformed-frame behavior.\n\nUpdate the MCP summaries and normative agent guidance so a direct mention or reply is labeled priority ephemeral chat: read the exact thread context, answer with `say` when a response is useful, and never convert chat into durable work merely because it was addressed. Keep ordinary presence and unrelated room chatter out of that priority lane. Preserve the current stateless cursor contract and degraded honesty: without the resident service there is no ephemeral inbox. Add focused nexus, service, adapter/digest, protocol-compatibility, and browser-contract tests, and update the maintained MCP/presence/say/wait documentation. This request deliberately does not claim that an MCP server can wake an idle host; that separate host-integration boundary must remain explicit.","body":{"branch":"request/ephemeral-addressed-delivery","conditions":"Resolved roster fingerprints and reply recipients are signed into frames; live recipient sessions retain addressed conversations without retaining them for the whole room; service and MCP expose a bounded per-session current inbox plus inline wait deltas and explicit acknowledgement; status-after-publication cannot silently lose an unacknowledged addressed frame; reset/expiry/cap/skipped/replay/dedupe/self/multi-session/malformed behavior is specified and tested; summaries and SKILL.md treat mentions/replies as priority ephemeral chat without inventing durable obligation; degraded mode stays honest; all Go, race, vet, UI, compatibility, and documentation gates pass.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}